{%- comment -%}
  Upsell row: rendered only through Shopify's product recommendations endpoint,
  routes.product_recommendations_url?section_id=anvil-upsell-row&product_id=…&limit=…&intent=related|complementary.
  It has no presets, so merchants cannot add it to a page. snippets/anvil-pb-upsells.liquid (and any other upsell
  list) reads the <li data-anvil-product-id> items of [data-anvil-upsell-row] from the response; prices, the
  "hide products already in the cart" rule and the item limit are applied by that block. Renders nothing when
  Shopify returns no recommendations. This section is never part of a page's render tree, so card and list styles
  live in assets/anvil-pb-commerce.css, which every caller loads (the product upsells and complementary blocks,
  the cart drawer's upsells block).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if recommendations.performed? and recommendations.products_count > 0 -%}
  <ul class="av-upsells__list" role="list" data-anvil-upsell-row data-anvil-intent="{{ recommendations.intent }}">
    {%- for rec in recommendations.products -%}
      <li class="av-upsells__item" data-anvil-product-id="{{ rec.id }}">
        {%- render 'anvil-product-card-mini', product: rec, button: 'add', source_tag: 'upsell' -%}
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Upsell row",
  "class": "av-upsell-row",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
